The Gates are ours again. The hinges will never forgive us.

Thorin counted eleven goblins fled east across the Blackmelt river. Vala counted twelve. They have agreed to disagree, loudly, for the rest of the march.

The Blackmelt can only be crossed at the two old fords, and the goblins know it — their slingers are dug in on the far bank where the water narrows, with orc muscle lounging behind them. A sling stone can reach across the ford. An axe cannot.

Muni says: let them hold a river. Rivers are patient. Dwarves are more patient.

I say: the fords by nightfall. Wade careful — stones fly two spans, and the water gives no cover at all.
